"""Read-only follow-up for the final streaming/publishing rights boundary."""
import json,shutil,subprocess,time
from pathlib import Path
repo=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]; out=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
diff=subprocess.check_output(['git','diff','--','backend/defence_studio/services/package.py','backend/defence_studio/services/youtube.py','backend/tests/test_render_rm5.py'],cwd=repo,text=True)
prompt='''Independent read-only follow-up. Read/Grep/Glob only; never write or run commands, never access .env/credentials or providers. Prior review found core rights rechecks and queued-rights ordering correct. We then reproduced a remaining streaming-publisher bypass: _video_path read a package directly without the package download rights gate. publishing-rights-before.log: 1 failed DID NOT RAISE. Now a shared verify_package_asset_rights helper gates package_file, publishing preflight, _video_path, and post-upload/visibility stages. _upload checks the path before credential/provider access. Review the final changed source for concrete correctness/security defects, worker failure transitions, state semantics, and test validity. Read any relevant source/tests. Do not claim external Google or legal verification. New focused publishing-rights-after.log: 1 passed exit 0,13.82s. Full mocked Google suite and final export suites still running. Fresh-process rights-restart-check.json now checks the real revoked artifact's streaming path too (exit0). Do not claim full regression passed before its results. Return precise severity/file/line for actionable findings, or none. This is static review only.\n'''+diff
prompt+='\nFresh-process evidence:\n'+(out/'rights-restart-check.json').read_text()
prompt+='\nDisposition follow-up: your prior medium finding is retained in claude-publishing-review-before.txt. Reproduced actual worker FAILED_RETRYABLE vs expected FAILED_FINAL in publisher-state-before.log (1 failed). Current _advance catches IntegrationStale (including YtConflict), writes FAILED_FINAL/precondition, and preserves terminal states if cancellation wins. Explicit legal FAILED_FINAL transitions were added for active/waiting/post-upload states, without force. Regression publisher-state-after.log: 1 passed, exit0,40.50s. It drives the persistent worker across eight active states, verifies no provider access and no re-entry, plus cancellation winning inside the rights gate. Please verify this medium finding and low test-gap disposition against final source/tests and identify any remaining actionable defect. Broad clean backend completed 660 passed,5 skipped,exit0 but predates this final branch; final targeted publishing lifecycle rerun is running. Do not claim final tests finished until evidence exists.'
start=time.monotonic()
p=subprocess.run([shutil.which('claude'),'--print','--no-session-persistence','--permission-mode','plan','--tools','Read,Glob,Grep','--allowedTools','Read,Glob,Grep'],input=prompt,text=True,encoding='utf-8',capture_output=True,cwd=repo,timeout=600)
(out/'claude-publishing-review.txt').write_text(p.stdout,encoding='utf-8')
(out/'claude-publishing-review.stderr').write_text(p.stderr,encoding='utf-8')
(out/'claude-publishing-review-result.json').write_text(json.dumps({'exit':p.returncode,'seconds':time.monotonic()-start,'tools':'Read,Glob,Grep','mode':'plan'},indent=2))
print('Publishing review exit:',p.returncode)
